35,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The ledger shows a quarter less funding, and off-site contacts earn nothing. We must prioritize on-site programs to generate revenue.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The trial worked, then vanished. The booking system erases unstructured care. We are funding a ghost.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Midori,,Nine unfilled posts and rising agency costs are alarming. Yet midwifery has slack. Could we balance the load by shifting duties there?,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"The car park fills by eleven, and the shuttle misses most villages. If we add more patients, the whole place will just seize up.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shizue,,Those minutes show a joint clinic collapsing in a year. The data agreements took fourteen months. We cannot rely on partners who never truly signed up.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"Shion, your data confirms my fear. We are funding a ghost. With reduced funds, we must focus on on-site care that actually generates revenue.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shion,,"Jonathan, you’re chasing revenue while I’m chasing evidence. The trial proved the model works; the system just fails to record it. We need to fix the tracking, not the budget.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, I hear you, but the agency costs are bleeding us dry. We can’t fix tracking if the teams are already exhausted.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, exhausted teams are bad, but a full car park is worse. If we can’t park or book, no one gets in.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, I understand the physical strain. But if the partners vanish, the space is empty. We must secure the people before the parking.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shion, fixing tracking costs money we don’t have. With a quarter less funding, we need immediate, billable on-site activity to sustain the program.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, you’re confusing absence with failure. The trial worked; the records didn’t. We need a program that actually exists in the data, not just in your ledger.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Jonathan, I understand the budget pressure. But if we ignore the staffing crisis, the program will collapse under the weight of agency costs.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Shion, if the system doesn’t record it, it’s invisible to me. I can’t manage what I can’t see. We need visible slots to keep the flow moving.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Shion, I agree. If the records don’t show it, it’s fragile. We need a program that stands on its own, not on shaky external promises.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I hear the staffing and tracking concerns. But with reduced funds, we need a program that is billable, on-site, and sustainable. What specific on-site model addresses these gaps?","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, a model that logs every interaction. If it isn’t in the system, it didn’t happen. We need visibility, not just revenue.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Midori,,"@Jonathan, a model that uses the midwifery slack to support therapy. It balances the load and keeps us within budget.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Jonathan, I need a model with fixed, bookable slots. If it’s not in the system, I can’t manage the flow.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Jonathan, a model where our own staff hold the rota and budget. No outside partners to vanish, no shaky agreements. Just steady, internal care.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
